<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Milindapanha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Questions of King Milinda, Milinda Pañha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Milindapanha, or Questions of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menander-i">Milinda</a>, is a Buddhist text in Pali, probably compiled between the 1st century BCE and the 2nd century CE. It records a dialogue in which the monk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasena">Nagasena</a> answers the questions of King Milinda, identified with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-greek-kingdom">Indo-Greek</a> king Menander I, on rebirth, the self and other points of doctrine. It is highly regarded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theravada-buddhism">Theravada Buddhism</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/milindapanha.jpg" alt="Milindapanha" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Folios_of_the_Bhikkhuni-patimokkha_(BL_IO_Man.Pali_21).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
